   "about": "Reviews protections for young workers and industrial discipline, then indexes labor laws for possible revival or amendment.",
   "summary": "The concluding chapters describe prewar child labor protections, their wartime erosion, and laws used to control workers and suppress independent organizing. They recommend restoring minimum age and safety rules, repealing coercive legislation, protecting union activity, and loosening employers’ control of factory dormitories. The appendix lists relevant factory, mining, seamen’s, and child protection laws, with section-by-section recommendations.",
