   "about": "Assesses Imperial Household assets and proposes how Military Government should secure and administer them.",
   "summary": "The report proposes a Crown Property Custodian, inventories, controls on transfers, supervision of productive land, and safeguards for financial assets, records, and palaces. Its opening chapters explain the legal distinction between hereditary and ordinary crown property and estimate the extent, value, and income of forests, farmland, securities, estates, and other holdings. It examines the Imperial Household’s shares in the Bank of Japan and Yokohama Specie Bank, while cautioning that the recommendations were largely drafted before Japan’s surrender.",
